 i can buy a house at  18. and then i thought well hold on i'm  17.  if i stick it to someone else's name i  could do it right now  so it was it was kind of the the  obstacle the dagger in the chest  that actually helped me and enabled me  to get my first property when i was 17.  so how i bought it  it was on um on the maryvale road in  birmingham bourneville  i still own the house i still own the  house today and it was  by the time i actually completed on it  was the week before my 18th birthday  and i was i was 17 years old and i  bought it with the banks money it was it  was it was a no money down  um um property where you buy it we  financed the same day i bought it for a  hundred thousand pounds  we financed it the same day 120  um pulled the money out i did it in my  step dad's name he didn't give me any  money but he just let me let me host the  property  and everyone was saying to me at the  time property markets crashing right now  what are you  doing it's going to go down the  properties are going to be worth 5  thousand pounds  um people are saying to me that's a bad  time what are you doing getting all  these  mentors and getting all these courses  why don't you just go to university and  spend 40 000 pounds learning about art  you know that that's people's mindset so  a lot of people were against me the  press were against me at the time not  against me as a person but against the  idea of being a buy to that landlord  everyone was saying viceland is dead  bought the house my mortgage payments  were 166 pounds per month  on that little house and what i did and  i could literally write a book on my  first house  what i did was i rented it out room by  room  as a multi-let at the time i didn't know  what i was doing i didn't know that  um this was a hmo and this was i just  thought actually you know what  if i rent it out by the room i'll get  more rent there was two reception rooms  three bedrooms i turned one of the  reception rooms into a bedroom by  